  "evidence_notes": "Rachel, 31, has Crohn's, endometriosis, and chronic fatigue syndrome. She was diagnosed five years ago after experiencing fatigue and stomach issues. She tried mesalamine and azathioprine with minimal improvement. She then started Remicade, which worked for a year before she had an allergic reaction. She switched to Humira, which provided about 50% improvement. Methotrexate was added, but she experienced hair loss. She then started Stelara, which was initially denied by insurance but eventually approved and she has been on it for eighteen months, finding it \"okay, not great, just okay.\" She is considering experimental treatments and clinical trials, and her doctor is discussing combination therapy with Stelara and methotrexate. She is also considering surgery but is hesitant."
